  "body": "Grandstand views, serious scale and flexibility rarely come together this well. This substantial weatherboard home spans more than 400sqm over three spacious levels, capturing sweeping views across Rangitoto and the Hauraki Gulf, taking in Milford Beach and reserve, the marina, Takapuna and the Auckland skyline.\r\n\r\nThe real attraction is the way the home can work for different stages of life. There is excellent connection between the levels, while practical separation creates options for extended family, an au pair, live-in nurse or additional income. \r\n\r\nThe top level is fully self-contained and set up to generate income, while the lower level could provide another independent living option.\r\n\r\nAlternatively, live comfortably on the main level in an apartment-style setup and lock up and leave when travelling, with the additional spaces helping towards the mortgage or funding your adventures.\r\n\r\nHigh-stud ceilings, a modern kitchen and excellent indoor-outdoor flow define the main living level, opening to generous covered and uncovered entertaining areas where sunny afternoons and BBQs can be enjoyed.\r\n\r\nOutside, the grounds are sunny, private and easy care, while the large tandem garage includes a useful hobby room or storage area, with plenty of off-street parking for boats and additional vehicles.\r\n\r\nAnd the location is hard to beat. Walk to Milford Beach, the bowling club, marina or Milford Village for shopping, cafés and restaurants. Schooling is equally well catered for, with Campbells Bay Primary, Murrays Bay Intermediate, Wairau Intermediate and Westlake Boys and Girls High Schools all zoned, plus St Joseph's, Rosmini and Carmel College nearby.\r\n\r\nBig on views. Big on space. Big on possibilities.\r\n\r\nTo view property files, please follow this link: https://www.harcourtsfiles.co.nz/listings/K9I1",
